data: {"choices":[{"delta":{"reasoning_content":"Static source review looks good so far:\n- `App.jsx` uses `AppShell`, `Header`, `Footer`, `Button` from `@codesweep-ai/ui` — matches design building blocks.\n- Greeting: exact \"Hello, world!\" as `h1`, `style={{ color: var(token) }}` — token-driven.\n- Buttons: Blue→--color-cat-1, Orange→--color-cat-6, Violet→--color-cat-5 — matches design table.\n- Default `useState(COLOURS[0].token)` = Blue — matches.\n- `variant=\"secondary\"`, `size=\"md\"` — matches.\n- Footer text \"Built with the codesweep design system\" — matches.\n- Header title \"Colour Greeting\", no nav props — matches.\n- index.css: content centered flex column, gap from `--space-6` token, button-row centered with `--space-3` gap; greeting font-size/weight from tokens. No hex anywhere in src — let me grep to confirm.\n- package.json lists `@codesweep-ai/ui` ^0.3.0.\n\nNow let me check for hex values in the app source, then npm install, build, serve, and check the served page. I need to verify:\n1. data-component attributes for Header, Footer, Button in the served HTML.\n2. That clicking buttons changes colour — this requires a browser/DOM. Let me see what's available (node, maybe a headless browser like playwright or puppeteer?). I should check what's available in the environment.\n\nLet me proceed with npm install first, and in parallel check for hex values."},"finish_reason":null,"index":0,"raw_output":null}],"created":1793343710,"id":"chatcmpl-6a1b37e7","model":"accounts/fireworks/models/kimi-k3","object":"chat.completion.chunk","usage":null}

